{"name":"Bottled Ship","hex":"#9b6944","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"bottled","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["simple past and past participle of bottle"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Packaged in a bottle.","drunk"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/bottled"},{"term":"ship","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A water-borne vessel generally larger than a boat.","A vessel which travels through any medium other than across land, such as an airship or spaceship."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To send by water-borne transport.","To send (a parcel or container) to a recipient (by any means of transport)."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/ship"}],"entries":[{"title":"Bottle","blocks":[{"text":"A bottle is a narrow-necked container made of an impermeable material in various shapes and sizes that stores and transports liquids. Its mouth, at the bottling line, can be sealed with an internal stopper, an external bottle cap, a closure, or induction sealing."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/Bouteille.jpg/330px-Bouteille.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bottle","wikidata":"Q80228"},{"title":"Ship","blocks":[{"text":"A ship is a large watercraft designed for travel across the surface of a body of water, carrying cargo or passengers, or in support of specialized tasks such as warfare, oceanography and fishing. Ships are generally distinguished from boats, based on size, shape, load capacity and purpose. Ships have supported exploration, trade, warfare, migration, colonization, and science. Ship transport is responsible for the largest portion of world commerce."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/30/Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolten.4.phb.ajb.jpg/330px-Containerterminal_Altenwerder_%28Hamburg-Altenwerder%29.Iris_Bolt